abstract: >
  Computational verification and simulation of spinor corrections b-C (Berry, 1st order)
  and a-C (braking, 2nd order) on the Klein quartic curve, with the unified Choptyuk
  formula. Enhanced v2.0 includes: 4D spin manifold extension, Kähler surface corrections
  (K3 hyperkähler, Dolbeault correspondence), Tyukovsky equation adaptation (zero free
  parameters), Einstein GR QNM predictions (correction factor ≈ 0.999916), and comprehensive
  criticism response (b₂=22 uniqueness, stability, universality). v2.1.0 adds §14: the jet
  diffusion wake bridge (CMS HIN-25-012, arXiv:2602.19431, PRL 2026) connecting the GUE
  strong-CP suppression argument to the experimentally observed QGP diffusion wake, with the
  4D-PSL(2,7)/Hg-199 mass-ratio model producing the full scale bridge
  k=23 (10^-10 Strong CP) → k=28 (5σ CMS) → k=45 (10^-18 quark scale) → k=48 (thermalisation).
keywords:
  - "spinor correction"
  - "Klein quartic"
  - "Choptyuk formula"
  - "Dirac operator"
